    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0281" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1073: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-03T10:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">February 3,
                                1920—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 4—10:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Department’s January 31, 2 p.m. Yesterday afternoon the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs informed me that daily deposits had <pb facs="0282" n="192"
                        xml:id="pg192"/> been resumed and that he would answer my note, number
                        347,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d150-f1"/> in two or three days. I will cable its
                    substance when received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
